  data: {
    LLM: "If you hold a Ten, try to throw it on your partner's winning trick. If you hold the Jack of trumps, hide it until you are sure your partner can protect it.\n\nThe Low Strategy: Since 'Low' is taken, not dealt, you must win the trick it's in. If you have the 2 of trumps, don't lead it; hold it as an escape card or wait until you can win a trick with a higher trump to secure it.\n\nPitch Manipulation: If you are the Pitcher and hold the Ace and Ten of a suit, lead the Ace. You've fixed the trumps and secured 4 card-points toward 'Game' in one move.",
    Player: "If you hold a Ten, try to throw it on your partner's winning trick. If you hold the Jack of trumps, hide it until you are sure your partner can protect it.\n\nThe Low Strategy: Since 'Low' is taken, not dealt, you must win the trick it's in. If you have the 2 of trumps, don't lead it; hold it as an escape card or wait until you can win a trick with a higher trump to secure it.\n\nPitch Manipulation: If you are the Pitcher and hold the Ace and Ten of a suit, lead the Ace. You've fixed the trumps and secured 4 card-points toward 'Game' in one move.",
