    basic: "If you hold a Ten, try to throw it on your partner's winning trick. If you hold the Jack of trumps, hide it until you are sure your partner can protect it.",
    intermediate: "The Low Strategy: Since 'Low' is taken, not dealt, you must win the trick it's in. If you have the 2 of trumps, don't lead it; hold it as an escape card or wait until you can win a trick with a higher trump to secure it.",
    advanced: "Pitch Manipulation: If you are the Pitcher and hold the Ace and Ten of a suit, lead the Ace. You've fixed the trumps and secured 4 card-points toward 'Game' in one move.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Always count the trumps played. With only 24 cards dealt, knowing the remaining trumps is easier than in other games.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "In Lancashire, winning the Low point (the 'Taken Low') is often the difference between winning and losing a match.",
      },
